#### Company Description

Ubisoft is a global leader in video games, with teams spread across the four corners of the world who create original and memorable gaming experiences, from Assassin's Creed to Rainbow Six, including Just Dance and many more. We believe that diversity of perspectives drives progress for both players and teams. If you are passionate about innovation and want to push the boundaries of entertainment, join our adventure and help us create the unknown!

#### Job Description

As a **Senior Gameplay Animator** within the March of Giants team at Ubisoft Montréal, you will take charge of the entire gameplay animation process, from creating memorable character performances to integrating and refining them within the game's ability system. You combine a sharp instinct for gameplay with exceptional mastery of animation fundamentals, understanding how movement conveys both game mechanics and character personality. You will work within a passionate, multidisciplinary team determined to push the boundaries of the MOBA genre.

**What you will do:**

- Create **gameplay and cinematic animations (keyframe)** that comply with the art direction and **game design constraints**;
- Integrate your animations into the character system and validate that they function correctly;
- Plan your tasks and advance them proactively;
- Provide constructive feedback to your colleagues;
- Regularly perform gameplay testing;
- Collaborate closely with other animators, game designers and programmers to deliver features **on schedule and to the expected quality level**;
- Ensure the **final quality** of the animated features integrated into the game.

#### Qualifications

- Solid understanding of keyframe animation principles (**_keyframe_**), game engines, production pipelines and their constraints;
- Mastery of animation software (**Maya**);
- Experience with **Unreal Engine** and **Blueprints**;
- Excellent communication, multitasking and problem-solving skills;
- Experience with motion capture workflows.

**What to send us:**

- Please send us a **portfolio** of your best work along with your **resume** highlighting your education, experience and skills.

#### Company Description

Ubisoft is a global leader in video games, with teams spread across the world creating original and memorable gaming experiences, from Assassin’s Creed to Rainbow Six, Just Dance and many more. We believe that diversity of perspectives drives progress for both players and teams. If you are passionate about innovation and want to push the boundaries of entertainment, join our adventure and help us create the unknown!

#### Job Description

As a team lead at Ubisoft Montréal, you will support a team that improves development methods, continuous integration and delivery pipelines, build systems and the tools used to ship Rainbow Six.

You will work with the person responsible for technical direction and partner teams to reduce obstacles to development, improve the quality of deliverables and make releases more reliable. You will also support the gradual adoption of artificial intelligence in the team's ways of working.

**What you will do:**

- Lead and support the team in its work and the development of its members;
- Align the roadmap and priorities with the person responsible for technical direction;
- Prioritize initiatives according to their impact on productivity, quality and delivery reliability;
- Plan and track the team's work, taking dependencies into account;
- Identify obstacles in development methods with partner teams;
- Facilitate collaboration with development, quality assurance, online services, production and core technology teams;
- Verify the value of solutions for the teams that use them and how well they meet identified needs;
- Improve continuous build, integration and delivery practices, test automation, tooling and systems observability;
- Support the adoption of artificial intelligence for automation, problem investigation, code quality and faster feedback on work;
- Foster collaboration and continuous improvement within the team.

#### Qualifications

**What you bring to the team:**

- Experience managing and supporting a team in a software, technical or video game environment;
- Good understanding of continuous integration and delivery, build systems, automation and development tools;
- Ability to turn technical direction into a work plan with technical partners;
- Experience in planning, prioritizing and tracking deliveries, including managing dependencies;
- Comfort collaborating with multiple teams in a complex production environment;
- Knowledge of software quality practices, test automation, systems observability or internal tooling;
- Ability to coach team members and communicate clearly;
- Interest in practical uses of artificial intelligence in software development.

#### Company Description

Ubisoft is a global leader in video games, with teams spread across the four corners of the world who create original and memorable gaming experiences, from Assassin's Creed to Rainbow Six, including Just Dance and many more. We believe that diversity of perspectives drives progress for both players and teams. If you are passionate about innovation and want to push the limits of entertainment, join our adventure and help us create the unknown!

#### Job Description

As a **Technical Director, Animation** at Ubisoft Montréal, you will join a small autonomous team developing a multiplayer experience in Unreal Engine. You will guide the development of animation systems that are fluid, expressive and high-performing, while ensuring alignment between creative goals and technical constraints.

You will work closely with the animation, rigging, programming and tools teams to create reliable and scalable production pipelines suited to the ambitions of the project.

**What you will do:**

- **Design**, implement and maintain high-performing and scalable **animation production pipelines**;
- **Collaborate** with the tools team to develop and improve **MotionBuilder** scripts in **Python**;
- **Work** with animators and programmers to refine **animation systems** in the game engine;
- **Support** the implementation of **procedural animation systems** and **full-body IK** systems;
- **Ensure** that animation systems support **character customization**;
- Balance **artistic quality** and **technical performance**;
- **Document** workflows, tools and processes intended for animation teams;
- **Provide** daily support to technical animators and animation teams;
- **Facilitate** collaboration between creative and technical teams;
- **Guide** teams in developing sustainable and efficient workflows.

#### Qualifications

- Experience in **technical animation**, in developing **animation systems** or in **programming** within the video game industry;
- Experience coaching or leading teams in a collaborative environment;
- Experience on live multiplayer games;
- Strong proficiency in **Unreal Engine** and 3D software such as **MotionBuilder**, **3ds Max** and **Maya**;
- Experience with scripting languages such as **Python**, **C#**, **JavaScript** and **MaxScript**;
- Understanding of **motion capture**, **state machines** and animation flows;
- Familiarity with **Jira**, **Perforce** or similar production tools;
- Excellent communication, collaboration and problem-solving skills.

**What to send us:**

- Your résumé highlighting your skills.
- Portfolio or projects relevant to the role.
